WEBVTT

00:03.628 --> 00:05.129
(footsteps approach)

00:05.131 --> 00:06.697
You, uh, got a minute, boss?

00:06.699 --> 00:08.098
Actually, I'm kind of busy.

00:08.100 --> 00:11.035
I'm pushing new code on an API
for this e-comm platform.

00:11.037 --> 00:12.586
"I am from the future.

00:12.588 --> 00:14.989
I am a handsome robot."

00:14.991 --> 00:16.624
Look, I-I wouldn't
bother you with this

00:16.626 --> 00:17.858
if I didn't think
it was important.

00:17.860 --> 00:19.310
Okay. Just make it quick.

00:19.312 --> 00:20.444
That's my specialty.

00:20.446 --> 00:21.878
Ask any woman
I've ever been with.

00:23.924 --> 00:25.838
I will call them both.

00:27.102 --> 00:28.085
What do you got?

00:28.087 --> 00:31.122
Behold your new

00:31.124 --> 00:32.440
coffee mug.

00:32.442 --> 00:34.625
(imitates crowd cheering)

00:34.627 --> 00:36.510
What?

00:36.512 --> 00:38.579
Remember? You asked me to look
for new mugs for your office.

00:38.581 --> 00:39.597
What do you think?

00:39.599 --> 00:41.382
Well, there's a hole on the top

00:41.384 --> 00:42.550
and no hole on the bottom.

00:42.552 --> 00:43.684
Nailed it.

00:43.686 --> 00:44.735
Thanks.

00:44.737 --> 00:45.903
Uh, so, uh, what do you want
written on it?

00:45.905 --> 00:47.488
Written on it?

00:47.490 --> 00:48.506
Uh, your choices are

00:48.508 --> 00:50.174
"Coffee," "Java" or "Joe."

00:50.176 --> 00:52.293
I don't know. Just...
Joe.

00:52.295 --> 00:53.460
Excellent choice.

00:53.462 --> 00:56.013
Although... what if
you hire a guy named Joe?

00:56.015 --> 00:57.815
I-I think the temptation
for these mugs

00:57.817 --> 00:59.850
to walk out the door
is a little too high.

00:59.852 --> 01:01.836
Fine.
Just write "Coffee" on it.

01:01.838 --> 01:03.470
Great!
Uh, coffee in the mug,

01:03.472 --> 01:05.556
and coffee on the mug.
Love it!

01:05.558 --> 01:06.557
Oh, uh...

01:06.559 --> 01:07.908
but, uh, let me run
this past you:

01:07.910 --> 01:10.411
"Java the Mug."

01:11.747 --> 01:14.081
You know, because of &lt;i>Star Wars.&lt;/i>

01:14.083 --> 01:14.915
Stop!

01:14.917 --> 01:16.250
Right.
Right.

01:16.252 --> 01:17.702
You're busy.
(laughs)

01:17.704 --> 01:19.003
Oh! Uh, one
last thing.

01:19.005 --> 01:20.738
Oh, good God!
Alan,

01:20.740 --> 01:22.089
I hired you as my assistant

01:22.091 --> 01:23.924
so I don't have to think
about things like this.

01:23.926 --> 01:24.875
Oh, yeah, I know,

01:24.877 --> 01:26.277
but I want to do
a good job for you.

01:26.279 --> 01:27.762
I mean, you're gonna look
at this every day

01:27.764 --> 01:28.996
and I don't want you
to hate it.

01:28.998 --> 01:30.381
That does happen with things

01:30.383 --> 01:31.999
I look at every day.

01:32.001 --> 01:34.185
Okay, so one
final question:

01:34.187 --> 01:37.104
do you want your mug to be
left-handed or right-handed?

01:40.442 --> 01:41.959
You're kidding, right?

01:41.961 --> 01:43.878
No, some people hold 'em
in their left hand,

01:43.880 --> 01:46.480
some people hold 'em
in their right hand.

01:47.699 --> 01:49.900
Mm-hmm.

01:54.289 --> 01:55.973
(dramatic gasp)
Wow.

01:55.975 --> 01:57.525
Okay. Okay.

01:57.527 --> 01:59.777
Changing your mug
from "World's Greatest Boss"

01:59.779 --> 02:01.679
to "World's Smartest Boss."
Okay.

02:01.681 --> 02:03.114
I'm gonna go pee.

02:03.116 --> 02:04.965
Oh, oh, as long as you're
in the bathroom, uh,

02:04.967 --> 02:07.885
I left three different types of
toilet tissue in there for you.

02:07.887 --> 02:10.304
Uh, let me know
which one is best.

02:10.306 --> 02:14.225
Oh! And the brown one
is not a joke.

02:14.227 --> 02:16.060
"Hire me, Walden.
I can be your assistant."

02:16.062 --> 02:19.397
You know what your mug should
say? "World's Worst Employee."

02:22.084 --> 02:24.916
Oh, World's Second
Worst Employee.

02:24.917 --> 02:28.917
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 11x03 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">This Unblessed Biscuit&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on October 10, 2013

02:28.942 --> 02:33.942
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

02:38.488 --> 02:40.706
Hey, nap time's over.

02:40.708 --> 02:41.941
I'm not napping.

02:41.943 --> 02:43.576
I threw my back out.

02:43.578 --> 02:45.344
My God, are you okay?
What happened?

02:45.346 --> 02:49.448
It seized up when I was climbing
into your bed to take a nap.

02:49.450 --> 02:52.118
Okay, uh,
everything's gonna be okay.

02:52.120 --> 02:53.286
Just... relax.

02:53.288 --> 02:54.787
Alan, get up here!

02:54.789 --> 02:56.122
Why are you calling Zippy?

02:56.124 --> 02:57.757
He's a chiropractor--
he can help.

02:57.759 --> 02:59.058
(laughs)
Oh, stop.

02:59.060 --> 03:01.861
It hurts when I laugh.
(chuckles) Oh.

03:01.863 --> 03:03.796
Has this happened before?

03:03.798 --> 03:06.165
Once. At a bike rally
in Sturgis.

03:06.167 --> 03:09.135
Me and a couple of Hells Angels
decided to drop acid

03:09.137 --> 03:10.870
and get naked.

03:11.338 --> 03:13.539
Alan!

03:13.541 --> 03:14.840
What's going on?

03:14.842 --> 03:16.208
Is something wrong?

03:16.210 --> 03:17.510
Berta threw her back out.

03:17.512 --> 03:19.278
Oh, no. What should we do?

03:19.280 --> 03:20.846
Well, I called
a chiropractor.

03:20.848 --> 03:22.415
Great.

03:23.617 --> 03:25.318
Oh, me! Oh...

03:25.320 --> 03:26.452
Duh.
(chuckles)

03:26.454 --> 03:28.187
Well, uh, let's see
what we got here.

03:28.189 --> 03:29.322
Where's the pain?

03:29.324 --> 03:32.224
Standing in front of me
asking stupid questions.

03:32.226 --> 03:34.360
Berta, be nice.
Alan's a doctor.

03:34.362 --> 03:36.495
(laughing):
Oh. Oh.

03:36.497 --> 03:37.863
Yes, yes, ha-ha.

03:37.865 --> 03:39.332
But I can help you.

03:39.334 --> 03:41.434
Although I am legally
obligated to tell you

03:41.436 --> 03:42.735
my license has expired.

03:42.737 --> 03:44.553
But thankfully backs
haven't changed that much

03:44.555 --> 03:46.939
since my unsuccessful
board review. (chuckles)

03:46.941 --> 03:48.924
So, uh, you can't
move at all?

03:48.926 --> 03:50.860
Every time I do,
it tightens up more.

03:50.862 --> 03:52.395
Oh, sounds
like a classic back spasm.

03:52.397 --> 03:54.497
You probably just need
bed rest and ice, uh,

03:54.499 --> 03:57.033
but, just in case, let me see
if you need a spinal adjustment.

03:57.035 --> 03:58.934
Touch me and you die.

03:58.936 --> 04:02.488
(quietly): She may also need
an attitude adjustment.

04:02.490 --> 04:05.408
Okay, I'll call my doctor and
have him come take a look.

04:05.410 --> 04:08.110
(scoffs) Western medicine. He'll probably
just prescribe pain killers.

04:08.112 --> 04:09.412
Call him.

04:09.414 --> 04:11.697
I will. In
the meantime,

04:11.699 --> 04:13.115
you stay here as
long as you need.

04:13.117 --> 04:14.333
I'll take the guest room.

04:14.335 --> 04:17.636
Why? My back's out
but my front still works.

04:17.638 --> 04:21.223
Be like Sturgis all over again.

04:21.225 --> 04:23.426
(chuckles)
Oh...

04:25.178 --> 04:26.512
Morning.

04:26.514 --> 04:28.147
Hey.

04:28.149 --> 04:30.399
Hey, were you alone last night?

04:30.401 --> 04:31.417
Yeah, why?

04:31.419 --> 04:34.737
Because from 11:15 to 11:22,

04:34.739 --> 04:36.822
all I heard was, "Oh, yeah,

04:36.824 --> 04:39.775
that's the way Daddy likes it."

04:40.594 --> 04:44.663
Oh, um...

04:44.665 --> 04:47.616
Uh, right, the-the walls
are really thin,

04:47.618 --> 04:49.668
uh, between my bedroom
and the guest room,

04:49.670 --> 04:52.088
and I-I was watching TV.

04:52.090 --> 04:53.389
Hmm.

04:53.391 --> 04:56.392
So the same show
came on again at 1:30

04:56.394 --> 04:58.277
and then again at 4:15?

04:58.279 --> 05:00.129
Huh.
(scoffs)

05:00.131 --> 05:02.515
Weird.
(chuckles)

05:02.517 --> 05:04.116
Can I ask you something?

05:04.118 --> 05:05.101
Mm-hmm.

05:05.103 --> 05:07.937
What is wrong with Daddy?

05:07.939 --> 05:10.639
He's lonely, okay?

05:10.641 --> 05:12.725
Can you just let it go?

05:12.727 --> 05:14.843
I should ask you
the same question.

05:16.846 --> 05:18.280
What are you doing?

05:18.282 --> 05:19.982
Well, since Berta
is incapacitated,

05:19.984 --> 05:23.202
I have taken the initiative to
design and build a chore wheel.

05:23.204 --> 05:24.520
What is a chore wheel?

05:24.522 --> 05:27.239
It is a wheel with a variety
of chores on the outside

05:27.241 --> 05:28.791
and names on the inside.

05:28.793 --> 05:30.326
I got the idea
from my brother Charlie,

05:30.328 --> 05:32.128
who had a whore wheel.

05:34.364 --> 05:36.315
The only name on it is "Walden""

05:36.317 --> 05:40.119
Ah, that's because it was my
chore to make the chore wheel.

05:40.121 --> 05:41.804
And your
first chore

05:41.806 --> 05:43.255
is...

05:43.257 --> 05:44.707
"cleaning Alan's room."

05:44.709 --> 05:46.091
(sucks air through teeth)
Ooh.

05:46.093 --> 05:49.411
That's gonna be tough
after last night.

05:50.213 --> 05:53.048
Maybe you should
have Daddy do it.

05:56.069 --> 05:59.188
Whoa, somebody found my stash.

05:59.190 --> 06:01.390
Wasn't hard.
It was right here in this box

06:01.392 --> 06:04.643
that says "Not Pot."
(chuckles)

06:04.645 --> 06:06.362
Very clever.

06:06.364 --> 06:08.197
I didn't want anybody
to find my pot.

06:08.199 --> 06:09.582
I was about to write, uh,

06:09.584 --> 06:12.751
"This Box Contains
Poisonous Jumping Bugs,"

06:12.753 --> 06:14.954
but then I thought,
"What if this magic marker

06:14.956 --> 06:16.872
"is actually magic
and it turns my pot

06:16.874 --> 06:19.425
into poisonous jumping bugs?"

06:19.427 --> 06:21.177
(chuckles)

06:21.179 --> 06:22.744
I was really high.

06:22.746 --> 06:24.930
Uh, you know, I-I really
don't think it's a good idea

06:24.932 --> 06:27.249
to mix marijuana
with muscle relaxers.

06:27.251 --> 06:28.851
Oh, those pills are long gone.

06:28.853 --> 06:30.970
What? You had a good
two weeks' worth.

06:30.972 --> 06:33.389
Or a great one night's worth.
(chuckles)

06:33.391 --> 06:35.374
Oh, bacon.

06:35.376 --> 06:37.960
You guys take
such good care of me.

06:37.962 --> 06:39.745
That's because
you take good care of us.

06:39.747 --> 06:42.565
That's because I love you guys.

06:42.567 --> 06:44.617
I love you more. Shh!

06:44.619 --> 06:46.468
How's your back feeling?

06:46.470 --> 06:48.103
Actually, a lot better.

06:48.105 --> 06:50.322
I think I'm ready
to go back to work.

06:50.324 --> 06:51.740
Oh, really?
So you can get up?

06:51.742 --> 06:53.826
Absolutely.
(chuckles)

06:53.828 --> 06:55.811
Am I up?

06:55.813 --> 06:56.812
No.

06:56.814 --> 06:58.564
Damn.

06:58.566 --> 07:00.399
How 'bout now?

07:01.735 --> 07:03.419
Yep, looking good.

07:03.421 --> 07:05.204
Told you.

07:05.206 --> 07:08.424
Hey! Bacon!

07:12.562 --> 07:15.314
Why do these have windows?

07:17.751 --> 07:18.851
I don't need to see inside.

07:18.853 --> 07:21.887
I trust 'em to wash
and dry the clothes.

07:21.889 --> 07:23.439
You know,
when you think about it,

07:23.441 --> 07:25.691
a lot of appliances
have windows.

07:25.693 --> 07:26.975
Ovens,

07:26.977 --> 07:28.744
microwaves.

07:30.163 --> 07:33.732
Wait a minute. Are we watching
them or are they watching us?

07:33.734 --> 07:36.652
Got a little contact high
in there with Berta,

07:36.654 --> 07:38.787
did you?
Shh!

07:38.789 --> 07:40.656
(whispers):
Not in front of the washer.

07:43.176 --> 07:45.711
Hey, how old do you think
Berta is anyway?

07:45.713 --> 07:48.797
I don't even know
her last name.

07:48.799 --> 07:52.651
You know, I'm just thinkin',
I mean, she hurt her back.

07:52.653 --> 07:54.503
It's taking her
a while to recover.

07:54.505 --> 07:57.456
I mean, maybe this job's just
getting to be too much for her.

07:57.458 --> 07:58.340
Really?

07:58.342 --> 07:59.441
Yeah, I don't know.

07:59.443 --> 08:00.693
I mean, she's not getting
any younger,

08:00.695 --> 08:02.695
and it's a pretty
labor-intensive job.

08:02.697 --> 08:07.116
Why in the world do you wear
boys' husky underwear?

08:08.118 --> 08:10.402
Okay, you know how some
people trim the hedges

08:10.404 --> 08:12.154
to make the
tree look bigger?

08:18.295 --> 08:23.465
Well, I say stuff the tree
in a smaller yard.

08:24.301 --> 08:26.418
We, when the police
raid the house

08:26.420 --> 08:28.337
and find a drawer full
of boys' underwear,

08:28.339 --> 08:30.389
that's not gonna be good
for any of us.

08:30.391 --> 08:32.141
Neither is a drawer full of pot.

08:32.143 --> 08:36.261
That's why I wrote
"Not Pot" on it.

08:36.263 --> 08:39.131
So are you saying you think
it's time for Berta to retire?

08:39.133 --> 08:41.533
I don't know.
Everyone slows down eventually.

08:41.535 --> 08:43.719
Mmm, maybe you're right.

08:43.721 --> 08:46.905
Maybe it's time to put
the old girl out to pasture.

08:46.907 --> 08:50.576
Send her off
to the housekeeper farm upstate.

08:50.578 --> 08:53.195
That might not be the best way
to tell her.

08:53.197 --> 08:55.564
What? The-the farm
is a beautiful place.

08:55.566 --> 08:59.251
She can run out in the fields
with all the other housekeepers.

08:59.253 --> 09:01.870
There's sponges
and fabric softener

09:01.872 --> 09:04.340
as far as the eye can see.

09:04.342 --> 09:08.310
And the only dishes left in
the sink are made of chocolate.

09:08.312 --> 09:11.664
I may be a little
stoned, too.

09:11.666 --> 09:15.100
You ever hear
about the roommate farm?

09:18.188 --> 09:19.838
Berta.

09:19.840 --> 09:21.890
We got a little surprise
for you.

09:21.892 --> 09:23.609
Chuck Norris?

09:24.427 --> 09:27.730
Fried chicken,
cheesecake and beer.

09:27.732 --> 09:31.617
That's what my first husband
requested for his last meal.

09:31.619 --> 09:33.435
Am I dying?

09:33.437 --> 09:34.703
Oh, don't be silly.

09:34.705 --> 09:36.121
Do you like farms?

09:36.123 --> 09:37.489
What?
WALDEN: Oh.

09:37.491 --> 09:40.826
I-I think what he's trying
to say is,

09:40.828 --> 09:45.047
have you ever thought about
hanging up the old toilet brush?

09:45.049 --> 09:48.400
Raising that vest up
to the rafters?

09:48.402 --> 09:51.053
Oh, my God, you're firing me.

09:51.055 --> 09:53.172
(chuckles) No. I-I would
never fire you.

09:53.174 --> 09:54.640
I'm talking about retirement.

09:54.642 --> 09:55.708
Just kicking back,

09:55.710 --> 09:57.810
taking it easy,
getting high every day.

09:57.812 --> 09:59.645
I do that now.

10:01.131 --> 10:03.332
Besides, I can't afford
to retire.

10:03.334 --> 10:05.384
Well, what about that
pension plan I set up for you?

10:05.386 --> 10:07.469
I'll tell you
what happened to it: life.

10:07.471 --> 10:09.137
Your house needs a new roof,

10:09.139 --> 10:10.773
your grandson needs braces,

10:10.775 --> 10:13.842
your daughter's meth lab
explodes.

10:13.844 --> 10:15.160
What were you planning
on doing,

10:15.162 --> 10:16.528
working for the rest
of your life?

10:16.530 --> 10:19.998
Nah, I thought about, uh,
getting a villa in Tuscany.

10:20.000 --> 10:22.785
Then I said, "Nah,
I'll just hang around here

10:22.787 --> 10:26.088
and clean the skid marks
out of Zippy's underwear."

10:29.459 --> 10:31.043
How about this?

10:31.045 --> 10:35.013
What if you could make
the same money you're making now

10:35.015 --> 10:37.116
and never have to work again?

10:37.118 --> 10:38.851
One last job? I like it.

10:38.853 --> 10:40.619
Am I driving or shooting?

10:40.621 --> 10:43.138
No. You retire,

10:43.140 --> 10:45.641
and I'll pay you for
the rest of your life.

10:45.643 --> 10:47.776
You're gonna pay me
for doing nothing?

10:47.778 --> 10:49.611
Yeah. I call it
the Alan Harper Plan.

10:51.347 --> 10:53.115
Where's this coming from?

10:53.117 --> 10:56.301
Uh, we're-we're just...
worried about you.

10:56.303 --> 10:59.288
This is a tough job, especially
for a woman of your age.

10:59.290 --> 11:00.956
What?

11:00.958 --> 11:03.542
He said it's hard for a woman
your age to do this job.

11:03.544 --> 11:04.510
I heard him!

11:04.512 --> 11:05.794
Oh.

11:05.796 --> 11:07.663
I can do the job just fine.

11:07.665 --> 11:09.965
Really? Because you
basically bent over

11:09.967 --> 11:12.651
and haven't been able to get
out of bed for two days.

11:12.653 --> 11:16.171
So you just want to treat me
like some pathetic charity case

11:16.173 --> 11:17.673
you can throw money at.

11:17.675 --> 11:20.192
Oh, no-no one's saying
you're a charity case.

11:20.194 --> 11:21.560
Although, I, on the other hand,

11:21.562 --> 11:24.045
would be happy to be one
of Walden's Kids.

11:26.432 --> 11:29.034
I'm just trying to do
something nice for you.

11:29.036 --> 11:30.769
By giving me a handout?

11:30.771 --> 11:33.572
Unlike you, I've worked for
every cent I ever made.

11:33.574 --> 11:34.373
Excuse me?

11:34.375 --> 11:35.958
You got rich from one idea.

11:35.960 --> 11:38.460
You have no clue what it's like
to work for a living.

11:38.462 --> 11:41.113
Okay, I am not gonna apologize
for being successful.

11:41.115 --> 11:42.498
No, you are not,
my friend.

11:42.500 --> 11:43.999
Shut up!
Shut up!

11:44.001 --> 11:45.567
And please,
"work for a living"?

11:45.569 --> 11:47.836
You hurt your back trying
to take a nap!

11:47.838 --> 11:49.204
You know what?

11:49.206 --> 11:50.939
I don't have to take this crap.

11:50.941 --> 11:52.257
Well, that makes two of us.

11:52.259 --> 11:53.826
It's settled then. I quit.

11:53.828 --> 11:56.595
Oh, no! Where am I gonna find
someone to eat my food,

11:56.597 --> 11:59.748
smoke my pot
and sleep in my bed?!

11:59.750 --> 12:00.799
Oh...

12:00.801 --> 12:02.734
Shut up!

12:12.492 --> 12:15.044
(sighs) So what do you think?
Was I right, or what?

12:15.046 --> 12:17.246
Yes, Helen is great.

12:17.248 --> 12:18.647
Although I still
don't understand

12:18.649 --> 12:21.283
why we couldn't at least
&lt;i>interview&lt;/i> a topless maid.

12:21.285 --> 12:23.535
Or four.

12:23.537 --> 12:25.304
Will you forget
about the topless maids?

12:25.306 --> 12:27.139
I will never forget
about the topless maids.

12:27.141 --> 12:28.424
You saw the video.

12:28.426 --> 12:31.827
"The only thing dirty
in your house will be me."

12:31.829 --> 12:33.829
(door opening)

12:33.831 --> 12:34.897
Supper time, boys.

12:34.899 --> 12:36.098
Oh.
Oh.

12:36.100 --> 12:39.268
Helen, this lemonade
is delicious.

12:39.270 --> 12:41.837
That's because
I have a secret ingredient.

12:41.839 --> 12:43.072
Oh, really?
What-What is it?

12:43.074 --> 12:44.206
Love.

12:44.208 --> 12:46.342
Aw!
Oh!

12:46.344 --> 12:48.210
And, like, a pound of sugar.

12:48.212 --> 12:49.912
(sighs)

12:49.914 --> 12:52.081
Hey, you still
miss Berta?

12:52.083 --> 12:53.349
Miss Berta who?

12:53.351 --> 12:56.485
Hey, maybe that's her
last name, "Who""

12:56.487 --> 12:58.420
More like, "Who Cares."

12:58.422 --> 13:00.789
(laughter)

13:00.791 --> 13:03.125
Oh, my God, look at this!

13:03.127 --> 13:05.027
And for dessert,

13:05.029 --> 13:07.196
when your tummy
starts to rumble,

13:07.198 --> 13:09.431
there's Helen's apple crumble.

13:09.433 --> 13:10.532
(laughs)

13:10.534 --> 13:12.468
Shut your mouth.

13:12.470 --> 13:14.403
I won't.

13:14.405 --> 13:15.871
You shouldn't.

13:15.873 --> 13:17.339
(laughter)

13:17.341 --> 13:20.075
The only thing Berta ever made
with an apple was a bong.

13:20.077 --> 13:22.444
Oh, she sounds
like a hoot-and-a-half.

13:22.446 --> 13:23.345
(laughter)

13:23.347 --> 13:24.880
Well, enjoy, boys!

13:24.882 --> 13:27.082
Oh, no, no, no, no,
come join us.

13:27.084 --> 13:29.118
Oh.

13:29.120 --> 13:32.855
Well, thank you very much.

13:32.857 --> 13:33.872
Oh.

13:33.874 --> 13:35.107
The only thing sweeter

13:35.109 --> 13:38.744
than your manners
is my peach cobbler.

13:39.429 --> 13:42.230
Spoiler alert-- tomorrow night.

13:43.333 --> 13:46.568
Well, I will be a gobbler
of your cobbler.

13:46.570 --> 13:50.422
I am gonna stitch that
on a pillow.

13:52.492 --> 13:55.177
Oh, do you...
do you mind if I say grace?

13:55.179 --> 13:58.230
Oh.
Yeah, sure, go ahead.

13:58.232 --> 14:01.250
Uh, should I eat this unblessed
biscuit, or spit it out?

14:01.252 --> 14:02.551
Dear Lord,

14:02.553 --> 14:05.220
we thank you for
the food that we are

14:05.222 --> 14:08.057
about to receive,
and all of the other blessings

14:08.059 --> 14:10.109
that you have bestowed upon us.

14:10.111 --> 14:11.927
Hmm. That was beautiful.

14:11.929 --> 14:12.895
And we humbly ask

14:12.897 --> 14:15.097
that you help Alan and Walden

14:15.099 --> 14:16.615
find the path to righteousness.

14:16.617 --> 14:17.900
Wait.

14:17.902 --> 14:19.168
What?

14:19.170 --> 14:20.435
And lead them out

14:20.437 --> 14:23.939
of their sinful
homosexual lifestyles...

14:25.241 --> 14:26.742
...lest

14:26.744 --> 14:29.945
their souls burn
in the fiery pits of hell

14:29.947 --> 14:34.683
for all eternity
with all of the other Sodomites.

14:36.252 --> 14:37.669
Amen. Can I get
some sweet potatoes?

14:37.671 --> 14:39.872
Oh, sure.

14:40.924 --> 14:42.224
Alan?

14:42.226 --> 14:43.592
What? She already thinks

14:43.594 --> 14:46.345
we're gobbling
each others' cobblers.

14:49.983 --> 14:53.252
(humming)

14:53.254 --> 14:54.436
When you're finished
with that dish,

14:54.438 --> 14:56.071
just leave it,
and I'll take care of it.

14:56.073 --> 14:57.106
Oh, thank you, Colleen.

14:57.108 --> 14:58.323
No problem.

14:58.325 --> 15:00.526
I'm gonna go make the beds.

15:01.928 --> 15:03.579
I don't want
to spoil the surprise,

15:03.581 --> 15:05.864
but I'm pretty sure
she was carrying a little bag

15:05.866 --> 15:07.282
♪ of pillow chocolates.

15:07.284 --> 15:09.101
I have to admit,
she's pretty terrific.

15:09.103 --> 15:11.620
Right? I mean, she's
a good cook, she's punctual.

15:11.622 --> 15:13.355
She's accepting
of our lifestyle.

15:13.357 --> 15:18.527
There is no lifestyle to accept.

15:18.529 --> 15:20.212
But if things change,
it's nice to know

15:20.214 --> 15:21.797
we won't lose
a great housekeeper.

15:23.783 --> 15:26.085
(cell phone rings)

15:26.087 --> 15:27.469
That's-that's not me.

15:27.471 --> 15:28.871
Oh, uh, maybe it's Colleen.

15:28.873 --> 15:33.425
Um, Colleen?

15:33.427 --> 15:35.677
Oh, for the love of God,
just turn it off.

15:37.981 --> 15:39.965
Oh, dear.

15:39.967 --> 15:41.283
What?

15:41.285 --> 15:44.303
Look at this.

15:44.305 --> 15:45.687
Oh!

15:47.240 --> 15:50.175
Okay, I'm-I'm sure there's
a logical explanation for this.

15:50.177 --> 15:52.211
I mean, she's a...
she's a single woman,

15:52.213 --> 15:54.179
probably just trying
to protect herself.

15:54.181 --> 15:56.364
So, what's this one for?

15:57.650 --> 16:00.068
She has two guns?

16:00.070 --> 16:02.337
Uh...

16:02.339 --> 16:05.207
I count four...

16:05.209 --> 16:08.093
and what looks like a shank.

16:08.095 --> 16:10.395
Okay, you get to fire this one.

16:10.397 --> 16:11.880
COLLEEN:
Did I hear my phone?

16:11.882 --> 16:14.049
(screaming)

16:15.151 --> 16:17.886
Alan has something
he'd like to tell you.

16:19.923 --> 16:21.723
I think I made
a pillow chocolate

16:21.725 --> 16:23.959
in my boys' huskies.

16:25.094 --> 16:28.080
Okay. Well,
our last housekeeper,

16:28.082 --> 16:30.082
um, cleaned.
Mm.

16:30.084 --> 16:31.917
And, uh, sometimes
cooked for us.

16:31.919 --> 16:33.702
Is that something that
you're comfortable with?

16:33.704 --> 16:36.021
Sure. What would you like me
to cook?

16:36.023 --> 16:38.073
Oh, I-I don't know.

16:38.075 --> 16:40.209
For breakfast, I like pancakes.
Mm-hmm.

16:40.211 --> 16:44.613
Of course. &lt;i>Pancakes!&lt;/i>

16:44.615 --> 16:47.499
I'm... I'm-I'm sorry.

16:47.501 --> 16:48.934
You see
an African-American woman,

16:48.936 --> 16:50.636
and the first thing
you think is,

16:50.638 --> 16:52.888
"Aunt Jemima going to whip us up
some flapjacks."

16:52.890 --> 16:54.323
WALDEN:
Oh!

16:54.325 --> 16:56.058
No! No! No!
No, no. Um...

16:56.060 --> 16:57.943
Do I need
to bring my own bandana,

16:57.945 --> 17:00.279
or are you going
to supply me with one?

17:00.281 --> 17:02.147
Oh, I'm-I'm sorry.
We just, uh...

17:02.149 --> 17:03.815
You know, we really like pancakes.
Yeah.

17:03.817 --> 17:05.403
But, you know, I suppose
waffles are-are fine.

17:05.428 --> 17:06.236
Yeah, waffles.

17:06.237 --> 17:09.104
&lt;i>Chicken&lt;/i> and waffles?

17:09.106 --> 17:10.956
You know what? Let's...

17:10.958 --> 17:12.658
Let's just forget
breakfast.

17:12.660 --> 17:14.626
I'll just... I'll
just have coffee.

17:14.628 --> 17:16.044
How do you take it?

17:16.046 --> 17:17.446
Bla...

17:19.716 --> 17:21.550
I prefer tea.

17:22.969 --> 17:25.821
Um, so, are you okay
with doing laundry?

17:25.823 --> 17:28.257
Yeah. And I suppose
you want me

17:28.259 --> 17:32.144
to separate the whites
from the colors.

17:33.980 --> 17:36.164
Um, but you are aware

17:36.166 --> 17:38.300
you're applying for a
job as a housekeeper?

17:38.302 --> 17:40.769
Oh, so, now I don't know
why I'm here?

17:41.637 --> 17:43.989
Um, I'm not sure you do.

17:43.991 --> 17:46.742
What?!
Okay, okay. Let's...

17:47.977 --> 17:49.428
Everybody just calm down.

17:49.430 --> 17:51.280
Oh, so now I've got to calm down

17:51.282 --> 17:53.749
just because I was diagnosed
with schizophrenia?!

17:54.984 --> 17:57.452
Can you believe
these fools, Donny?

18:03.927 --> 18:07.629
Okay, I think we have all
the information we need.

18:07.631 --> 18:10.115
Mm-hmm.
Um... we'll be in touch.

18:10.117 --> 18:12.434
Great.

18:12.436 --> 18:14.920
Let me know
if you need any references.

18:16.823 --> 18:19.007
Oh, you all have a lovely home.

18:19.009 --> 18:21.176
(laughs)

18:22.745 --> 18:25.964
Donny, come on now!

18:28.484 --> 18:30.736
No, no. You know what?
I changed my mind.

18:30.738 --> 18:32.537
I don't want to
talk to Berta.

18:32.539 --> 18:35.190
Too bad. You wouldn't let
a topless maid make your bed,

18:35.192 --> 18:36.959
and now you've got
to lie in it.

18:37.944 --> 18:40.429
All right, well, I am
not going to apologize.

18:40.431 --> 18:41.546
You won't have to.

18:41.548 --> 18:43.531
She said if you made
an effort and came to her,

18:43.533 --> 18:45.550
that she'd be more
than happy to apologize to you.

18:46.502 --> 18:49.137
Zippy says you
want to apologize.

18:50.340 --> 18:52.641
See what I did there?
Can we come in?

18:52.643 --> 18:54.593
No, place is a mess.

18:54.595 --> 18:57.746
I was a jerk
to my housekeeper, so she quit.

18:57.748 --> 18:59.798
Okay, that's it.
I'm out of here.

18:59.800 --> 19:02.184
Oh, come on, Walden! Is it that
difficult to say you're sorry?

19:02.186 --> 19:04.436
It is when you have nothing
to say you're sorry for.

19:04.438 --> 19:07.022
Are you that clueless?
You hurt my feelings.

19:07.024 --> 19:10.158
You hurt &lt;i>my&lt;/i> feelings,
&lt;i>and&lt;/i> you smoked all my pot,

19:10.160 --> 19:13.412
so I had no way of not feeling
what I was feeling.

19:14.914 --> 19:16.248
Okay, okay,
dialogue is good.

19:16.250 --> 19:18.083
Now let's see if we can find
some common ground.

19:18.085 --> 19:18.900
You're an idiot.

19:18.902 --> 19:20.335
Agree.

19:22.171 --> 19:25.540
Look, I... I...

19:25.542 --> 19:28.743
was trying to help you
because I care about you.

19:28.745 --> 19:31.430
Not because I see you
as a charity case.

19:31.432 --> 19:33.699
And I'm sorry if you got
the wrong impression.

19:33.701 --> 19:36.251
I'm sorry I overreacted.

19:36.253 --> 19:38.136
Besides, I was so high,

19:38.138 --> 19:41.023
I thought
you were a talking dragon.

19:44.894 --> 19:48.430
It is really good stuff.

19:48.432 --> 19:51.867
That's the stuff I give
my grandkids at Christmas.

19:53.169 --> 19:56.705
It's funny cause I get it
from a guy named Jesus.

19:58.324 --> 20:00.775
So, what do you say?
Will you come back?

20:00.777 --> 20:02.811
I don't know.

20:02.813 --> 20:04.946
You may be right.

20:04.948 --> 20:08.166
I might not be able
to do everything I used to do.

20:08.168 --> 20:10.552
Well, we'll work around it,
right?

20:10.554 --> 20:12.804
Oh, absolutely.
What-whatever it takes.

20:13.823 --> 20:15.057
Deal?

20:15.059 --> 20:16.708
Deal.

20:16.710 --> 20:18.793
Come on in, I'll make
you a cup of coffee.

20:18.795 --> 20:20.445
(laughing)

20:24.300 --> 20:27.319
Not funny!

20:27.321 --> 20:29.187
Mm.

20:29.189 --> 20:31.406
(laughing)

20:35.578 --> 20:37.729
Still not funny!

20:48.806 --> 20:50.823
I'm glad you're back.

20:50.825 --> 20:54.160
Me, too, and I really appreciate
you getting me some help.

20:54.162 --> 20:56.246
It's the least
I could do.

20:56.248 --> 20:58.097
And I have to admit,

20:58.099 --> 20:59.882
Alan was right about
hiring a topless maid.

20:59.884 --> 21:02.051
Oh.

21:08.219 --> 21:11.805
If it wasn't in the hamper,
it's not going in the washer.

21:11.807 --> 21:14.140
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
